&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built &lt;strong&gt;LazyScrape&lt;/strong&gt;, a clean, lightweight web automation tool designed for mobile and low-power devices. It is a web scraper that allows users to input any URL and instantly extracts all readable paragraphs and text headers from that page, filtering out noisy background code and scripts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Inspiration
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a 16-year-old developer working entirely from a smartphone without a laptop, I noticed how hard it is to read and study long documentation pages on small screens. I wanted to build a distraction-free tool that strips away website layouts and presents pure data cleanly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  What I Learned
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During this build, I deeply mastered Python's file systems and web request logic using modern syntax. I learned how to structure backend code so that it works seamlessly with mobile-friendly HTML environments.&lt;/p&gt;

