&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Demo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Partner Technologies
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Hackathon Experience
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Routing every incoming user prompt to a frontier reasoning model is the fastest way to blow through your token budget and degrade p99 tail latency. With the release of Gemini 4 Argon on the Gemini platform, engineering teams have access to deep multi-step reasoning in &lt;code&gt;gemini-4-argon&lt;/code&gt; alongside high-throughput, low-latency execution in &lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt; and open-weights models running directly on cluster accelerators.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In most production applications, workload complexity follows a steep power law. Roughly 70% of requests involve classification, summarization, schema extraction, or straightforward retrieval that a fast tier handles in a few hundred milliseconds. The remaining 30% require multi-hop synthesis, complex code generation, or ambiguous constraint solving where &lt;code&gt;gemini-4-argon&lt;/code&gt; shines. Hardcoding a single model identifier in your application containers forces you to either overpay on simple queries or under-deliver on complex ones.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By building a centralized AI routing layer on &lt;a href="https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE)&lt;/a&gt; using the &lt;a href="https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/concepts/gateway-api" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GKE Gateway API&lt;/a&gt;, platform teams can classify prompt complexity at the ingress edge, route requests across Gemini tiers (&lt;code&gt;gemini-4-argon&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt;) and self-hosted &lt;a href="https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/concepts/about-gke-inference-gateway" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GKE Inference Gateway&lt;/a&gt; pools, and enforce automatic fallback when rate limits occur.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this article, I will break down the architecture of a multi-tier Gemini 4 Argon router on GKE, configure GKE Standard and Autopilot infrastructure with &lt;a href="https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/workload-identity" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Workload Identity Federation for GKE&lt;/a&gt;, and walk through the routing, health-check, and observability configurations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why static model bindings fail in production
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When application teams integrate directly with LLM endpoints inside dozens of individual microservices, three operational problems surface quickly:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unbounded token spend and latency inflation&lt;/strong&gt;: A microservice calling &lt;code&gt;gemini-4-argon&lt;/code&gt; for routine JSON formatting pays frontier token pricing and waits for deep reasoning chains when &lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt; would produce an identical schema in a fraction of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Scattered credential and quota management&lt;/strong&gt;: Managing Gemini platform API quotas, retry backoffs, and regional failover across 30 separate application repositories leads to inconsistent behavior during traffic spikes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No path to hybrid in-cluster offload&lt;/strong&gt;: When high-volume, low-complexity tasks could be served at fixed cost by an open-weights model running on GKE GPU or TPU node pools, application code tightly coupled to a single model string cannot shift traffic without code changes and redeployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Centralizing model routing behind a GKE Gateway and an intelligent router service decouples client microservices from the underlying model tier.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Multi-tier routing architecture on GKE
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this architecture, internal microservices send standard requests to a regional internal GKE Gateway (&lt;code&gt;gke-l7-rilb&lt;/code&gt;). The Gateway forwards traffic to an &lt;code&gt;ai-model-router&lt;/code&gt; service that evaluates request metadata or runs a fast complexity check before dispatching the request to one of three model tiers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tier 1 (Frontier reasoning)&lt;/strong&gt;: High-complexity tasks, code synthesis, and multi-step planning route to &lt;code&gt;gemini-4-argon&lt;/code&gt; on the Gemini platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tier 2 (Low-latency interactive)&lt;/strong&gt;: Routine summarization, classification, and structured extraction route to &lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt; on the Gemini platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tier 3 (High-throughput local)&lt;/strong&gt;: High-volume batch transformations and strict data locality workloads route to an in-cluster vLLM pool running Gemma 4 via GKE Inference Gateway.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is how the three tiers compare across production operating dimensions:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Routing tier&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Target model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Primary workload profile&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Fallback path on &lt;code&gt;429&lt;/code&gt; / timeout&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tier 1: Frontier reasoning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;gemini-4-argon&lt;/code&gt; (Gemini platform)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Multi-step planning, complex code synthesis, ambiguous root-cause analysis&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;us&lt;/code&gt; multi-region endpoint, then graceful downgrade to &lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tier 2: Low-latency interactive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt; (Gemini platform)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Real-time chat, structured extraction, classification, single-turn tool calls&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;us&lt;/code&gt; multi-region endpoint, then in-cluster open-weights pool&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tier 3: High-throughput local&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Open-weights (Gemma 4 via vLLM on GKE)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;High-volume entity tagging, PII scrubbing, fixed-cost background jobs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Burst overflow to &lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt; on the Gemini platform&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sample router later in this article implements the Tier 1 and Tier 2 location failover and the Tier 1 downgrade. The paths into and out of the in-cluster Tier 3 pool depend on your Inference Gateway setup and are left to your own dispatch logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Configuring Workload Identity and GKE compute
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To call the Gemini platform without distributing static service account keys, bind the &lt;code&gt;ai-model-router&lt;/code&gt; Kubernetes ServiceAccount directly to an IAM role using Workload Identity Federation for GKE. This works identically across GKE Standard and GKE Autopilot clusters running GKE &lt;code&gt;1.32&lt;/code&gt; or later with the GKE Gateway controller enabled (&lt;code&gt;--gateway-api=standard&lt;/code&gt;) and an active regional proxy-only subnet (&lt;code&gt;--purpose=REGIONAL_MANAGED_PROXY&lt;/code&gt;) in your VPC.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note on model identifiers and locations&lt;/strong&gt;: The examples below use &lt;code&gt;gemini-4-argon&lt;/code&gt; (Gemini 4 Argon) and &lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt; (Gemini 3.8 Flash) configured via environment variables (&lt;code&gt;PRO_MODEL&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;FLASH_MODEL&lt;/code&gt;). Both models are served from the &lt;code&gt;global&lt;/code&gt; endpoint and the &lt;code&gt;us&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;eu&lt;/code&gt; multi-region endpoints, not from individual regions such as &lt;code&gt;us-central1&lt;/code&gt;, so the router fails over from &lt;code&gt;global&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;us&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;PROJECT_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"production-ai-platform"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;PROJECT_NUMBER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;gcloud projects describe &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;PROJECT_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"value(projectNumber)"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;LOCATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"us-central1"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;CLUSTER_NAME&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"ai-gateway-cluster"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Point kubectl at the cluster&lt;/span&gt;
gcloud container clusters get-credentials &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;CLUSTER_NAME&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--location&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;LOCATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;PROJECT_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Create the namespace and Kubernetes ServiceAccount&lt;/span&gt;
kubectl create namespace ai-routing
kubectl create serviceaccount gemini-router-sa &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--namespace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;ai-routing

&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Grant the Kubernetes ServiceAccount permission to invoke Gemini platform models&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# (the underlying IAM role string is still roles/aiplatform.user)&lt;/span&gt;
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;PROJECT_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--member&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"principal://iam.googleapis.com/projects/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;PROJECT_NUMBER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;PROJECT_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;.svc.id.goog/subject/ns/ai-routing/sa/gemini-router-sa"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"roles/aiplatform.user"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--condition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;None
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  Provisioning capacity on GKE Autopilot vs. Standard
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the router Deployment itself, standard CPU compute is sufficient. If you also operate Tier 3 (in-cluster open-weights inference via GKE Inference Gateway for high-volume offload), configure your accelerator capacity according to your cluster mode:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GKE Autopilot with &lt;code&gt;ComputeClass&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Define a declarative &lt;code&gt;ComputeClass&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;cloud.google.com/v1&lt;/code&gt;) that requests NVIDIA L4 GPUs (&lt;code&gt;gpu.type: nvidia-l4&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;gpu.count: 2&lt;/code&gt;) with prioritized fallback from on-demand capacity to Spot VMs during regional stockouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GKE Standard node pools&lt;/strong&gt;: Create a dedicated GPU node pool (&lt;code&gt;gcloud container node-pools create vllm-l4-pool --cluster="${CLUSTER_NAME}" --location="${LOCATION}" --machine-type=g2-standard-24 --accelerator=type=nvidia-l4,count=2,gpu-driver-version=latest --enable-autoscaling --min-nodes=1 --max-nodes=6&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Implementing the Gemini 4 tier router
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;ai-model-router&lt;/code&gt; service inspects incoming requests, estimates task complexity (using explicit client headers, token count thresholds, or keyword triggers), and dispatches the call through the &lt;code&gt;google-genai&lt;/code&gt; SDK with cross-location failover and cross-tier fallback. It also exposes a &lt;code&gt;/healthz&lt;/code&gt; endpoint that both the Pod &lt;code&gt;readinessProbe&lt;/code&gt; and the GKE Gateway load balancer health check use to verify backend readiness.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Save the following implementation as &lt;code&gt;router_app.py&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fastapi&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;FastAPI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;HTTPException&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pydantic&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;BaseModel&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;google&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;genai&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;google.genai&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;types&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;google.genai.errors&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;APIError&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;app&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;FastAPI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;GKE Gemini 4 Argon Multi-Tier Router&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;PROJECT_ID&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;PRIMARY_LOCATION&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;PRIMARY_LOCATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;global&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;SECONDARY_LOCATION&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;SECONDARY_LOCATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;PRO_MODEL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;PRO_MODEL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;gemini-4-argon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;FLASH_MODEL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;FLASH_MODEL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Project-scoped Gemini platform clients authenticated through Workload Identity Federation for GKE.
# The vertexai=True flag is the SDK switch for project-scoped IAM auth instead of an API key.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;primary_client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;genai&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;vertexai&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;PROJECT_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;location&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;PRIMARY_LOCATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;secondary_client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;genai&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;vertexai&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;PROJECT_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;location&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;SECONDARY_LOCATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;REASONING_KEYWORDS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;architect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;debug&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;prove&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;multi-step&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;optimize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;trade-off&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;root cause&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;PromptRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;BaseModel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;system_instruction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;require_deep_reasoning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;select_model_tier&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;PromptRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routing_hint&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Selects the Gemini 4 Argon (frontier) or Gemini 3.8 Flash tier based on client hints and prompt characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routing_hint&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;pro&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;or&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;require_deep_reasoning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;PRO_MODEL&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routing_hint&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;flash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;FLASH_MODEL&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="n"&gt;prompt_lower&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;lower&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;word_count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;len&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;split&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;has_reasoning_trigger&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;kw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prompt_lower&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;REASONING_KEYWORDS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;word_count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;600&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;or&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;has_reasoning_trigger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;PRO_MODEL&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;FLASH_MODEL&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;build_config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;system_instruction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;types&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;GenerateContentConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Gemini 4 Argon ignores sampling parameters and defaults to the MEDIUM thinking level,
